<title>FRANCE: Alcatel has $9.6 mln Mozambique GSM deal.</title>
<headline>Alcatel has $9.6 mln Mozambique GSM deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom said it had been awarded a $9.6 million turnkey contract to supply a GSM mobile communication network to Telecomunicacoes de Mocambique (TDM).</p>
<p>The first phase of the project will cover the Greater Maputo area as well as connecting roads to South Africa and Swaziland AND is scheduled to begin commercial operation at the end of June 1997. Once completed, it will offer capacity to some 10,000 subscribers.</p>
<p>The network will be operated by TMN, in which TDM has a 74 percent stake and Deutsche Telekom GmbH unit DeTeCon the remaining 26 percent.</p>
</text>
